.TH ATOPHTTPD 1 "Oct 2026" "Linux"
.SH NAME
.B atophttpd
- A web style atop(https://www.atoptool.nl)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B atophttpd
[\-h] [\-d] [\-D] [\-H] [\-p PORT] [\-P PATH] [\-S SECONDS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I atophttpd
depends on atop and reads atop rawlog, provides web
service(HTTP 1.1). A user accesses atop by a web browser without
login permission of a server, it's also possible to get/analyze
statistics of many servers in batch.
The /metrics endpoint exports process TCP and UDP receive/transmit bytes per
second for Prometheus. Process metrics require atop process-network data
from a compatible collector and atop started with \-K. /health returns HTTP 200
when the latest sample is fresh and has process-network support, otherwise 503.

Since atophttpd access the rawlog of atop, this daemon requires the
permission of
.B PATH.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\-h
Print usage message.
.TP
\-d
Run in daemon mode.
.TP
\-D
Run with debug message. (not in daemon mode)
.TP
\-H
Hide cmdline for security protection. (Ex, mysql -pPASSWD)
.TP
\-p PORT
Listen to PORT, default 2867.
.TP
\-P PATH
Specify atop log path, default
.B
/var/log/atop.
.TP
\-S SECONDS
Override the Prometheus sample freshness limit. By default, it is the
greater of 30 seconds and twice the atop sample interval.
.TP
\-a ADDR
Bind HTTP to ADDR, default 127.0.0.1.
.TP
\-t[PORT], \-\-tls-port[=PORT]
Enable mutual TLS on PORT (default 2868). TLS support requires a build with USE_TLS=YES.
.SH METRICS
The /metrics endpoint returns interval gauges named
.B atophttpd_process_network_receive_bytes_per_second
and
.B atophttpd_process_network_transmit_bytes_per_second.
The labels are host, pid, name, start_time and protocol. Status gauges report
sample timestamp, interval, age, freshness and process-network availability.
If no complete sample is available, no process series are returned; a malformed
indexed sample returns HTTP 503. Do not apply Prometheus rate() to these gauges.
The /health endpoint checks freshness and availability without formatting
process series. /showsamp accepts the original lables query parameter and
labels as an alias.
.SH SOURCE
https://github.com/pizhenwei/atophttpd
